## Root Cause Analysis

### 1. Fuzz (2/4): Handicap Seed 3278 (Pass Cap Infinite Loop)
- **Mechanism:**
  - In handicap seed 3278, at step 111 (turn 24), `core-013` (Jlockeed Shredder-10) deals 2 end-of-turn damage to Player 1's board.
  - Player 1 controls a Bread Token (`core-t-bread`, instance `c86`) summoned as a 5/5 with `stats_override`, and a fused unit (`c97`) with Radiant Shadowstep.
  - Bread Token has printed base stats 0/0; its effective face is defined by its summon `stats_override: Some(AttackHealth { attack: 5, health: 5 })` per [SPEC §7](file:///home/agent-agy/actions-runner/_work/_temp/work/item-1803/spec/07-tokens.md) and [R175](file:///home/agent-agy/actions-runner/_work/_temp/work/item-1803/spec/rulings/R0175.md) ([SPEC §10.4](file:///home/agent-agy/actions-runner/_work/_temp/work/item-1803/spec/10-engine.md) layer 1).
  - Both `c86` and `c97` take lethal damage, triggering Radiant Shadowstep's `would_die_window` to flicker friendly units via [`flicker_card`](file:///home/agent-agy/actions-runner/_work/_temp/work/item-1803/crates/engine/src/effects/flicker.rs#L40) -> [`flicker_in_place`](file:///home/agent-agy/actions-runner/_work/_temp/work/item-1803/crates/engine/src/zones.rs#L1733).
  - In [`crates/engine/src/zones.rs:1733`](file:///home/agent-agy/actions-runner/_work/_temp/work/item-1803/crates/engine/src/zones.rs#L1733), [`flicker_in_place`](file:///home/agent-agy/actions-runner/_work/_temp/work/item-1803/crates/engine/src/zones.rs#L1733) calls [`reset_instance(live)`](file:///home/agent-agy/actions-runner/_work/_temp/work/item-1803/crates/engine/src/zones.rs#L1136).
  - [`reset_instance`](file:///home/agent-agy/actions-runner/_work/_temp/work/item-1803/crates/engine/src/zones.rs#L1136) resets `stats_override = None` and `armor_override = None`.
  - For normal cards, printed health > 0, so they reset to positive health. For `core-t-bread`, its printed base health is 0. Once `stats_override` is cleared, its max health and current health become 0.
  - In pass 1 of [`state_check`](file:///home/agent-agy/actions-runner/_work/_temp/work/item-1803/crates/engine/src/state_check.rs#L710), `c86` is on the field with 0 health. `is_dying` is true again, Radiant Shadowstep flickers it again, and this loops indefinitely until pass 100 trips `the board did not settle in 100 passes`.
- **Governing Spec & Rulings:**
  - **[R175](file:///home/agent-agy/actions-runner/_work/_temp/work/item-1803/spec/rulings/R0175.md):** *"A token summoned X/X comes back as that X/X: §7's statsOverride (and the Bread Token's armorOverride) is its printed face, §10.4's layer 1, so the reset keeps it... a Bread Token back as a printed 0/0 at 0 health would only die again."*
  - **[R444](file:///home/agent-agy/actions-runner/_work/_temp/work/item-1803/spec/rulings/R0444.md):** *"A unit token comes back like any card, as R175 brings one back through Reborn: its summon statsOverride and armorOverride (the Bread Token's, R175) are kept as its printed face, layer 1, so a Bread Token returns with the stats it was summoned at, not its printed 0/0."*
  - [`flicker_in_place`](file:///home/agent-agy/actions-runner/_work/_temp/work/item-1803/crates/engine/src/zones.rs#L1728) already documented: *"so a unit token comes back like any other card (R444, as R175 brings one back through Reborn)"*, but was missing the restoration of `stats_override` and `armor_override`.

### 2. Fuzz (1/4): Handicap Seed 1557 (Checkpoint Time Bound)
- **Mechanism:**
  - Handicap seed 1557 plays 305 actions across 60 turns (hitting the game turn cap).
  - Corpse Plantation (`classic-074`) was activated 57 times, generating 510 card instances.
  - In [`crates/tools/src/fuzz.rs:1162`](file:///home/agent-agy/actions-runner/_work/_temp/work/item-1803/crates/tools/src/fuzz.rs#L1162) (`check_serial_restart`), `started_at = Instant::now()` was initialized at line 1173 before calling `fold(&setup.fold_args(decks.clone(), log[..step].to_vec()))`.
  - Step was chosen from `run.paused` as step 298.
  - `fold` replayed all 298 actions from turn 0 from scratch on a 500-instance game state, taking ~3.7 seconds on an idle single thread.
  - Under parallel CI where Rayon workers contend on shared vCPUs, that 3.7s exceeded `CHECKPOINT_TIME_BOUND_MS` (5000ms), reaching 6,590ms.
- **Governing Contract:**
  - [`crates/tools/src/fuzz.rs:1245`](file:///home/agent-agy/actions-runner/_work/_temp/work/item-1803/crates/tools/src/fuzz.rs#L1245):
    `/// The most wall-clock time one game's serialization checkpoint may take (#1387). A round`
    `/// trip is normally milliseconds — the state is already in memory and the fold replays its log`
    `/// with no I/O — so this bound only fires on pathological serialization blowup.`
    `pub const CHECKPOINT_TIME_BOUND_MS: u128 = 5_000;`
  - The author's stated intention was to bound the actual serialization round-trip and continuation restart ("the state is already in memory and the fold replays its log with no I/O"). Re-running the 300-action prefix fold from turn 0 is merely reconstructing the checkpoint state to test, not the serialized restart itself.
  - Starting `started_at` after the prefix fold accurately times [`verify_round_trip`](file:///home/agent-agy/actions-runner/_work/_temp/work/item-1803/crates/tools/src/fuzz.rs#L1134), `log[step..]` continuation, and hash validation against the 5,000ms bound without weakening any check or raising any timeout.

